GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC9 §4): the side strips follow a window's outline past the screen's
edge.

- GPU2D_Soft: each line records where windows 0 and 1 are inside on the screen (none while
  windows are off). A strip pixel is inside a window when the window reaches that far past the
  edge: inside at the edge, its outline is followed from the nearest lines where it shows within
  the screen, continued at its own rate (a circle grazing the edge reaches a pixel or two past it,
  a wipe at the edge covers the strip). Replaces 0010's copy of the edge's window state across
  the whole strip.
- With the wider picture, a window inside up to column 254 with its end register at 255 (as far
  as it goes) also takes column 255: no one-pixel line between the screen and the right strip.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

